 "answer": "## Observed Facts\n\n- **Data Scope:** OpenStack, full corpus, 2017-05-14 19:39 to 2017-05-17 12:02 [E1]. Total: 207,820 Log Entries [E2].\n- **Level mix:** INFO 204,506; WARNING 3,118; ERROR 186; CRITICAL 2; no level 8 [E2]. Most entries (about 98%) are INFO, so the risk signal is concentrated in the small WARNING and ERROR share.\n- **ERROR, Component `oslo_service.periodic_task`:** 184 of 186 ERROR entries [E4]. Sampled messages read \"Error during ComputeManager._run_image_cache_manager_pass\" and \"InvalidDiskInfo: ... qemu-img failed to execute\" [E7][E12]. Daily counts: 139 on 2017-05-16 and 47 on 2017-05-17 [E10].\n- **WARNING, Component `nova.virt.libvirt.imagecache`:** 3,059 of 3,118 WARNING entries [E5]. Daily counts: 270 on 2017-05-14, 1,966 on 2017-05-16, 823 on 2017-05-17 [E11]. This is the largest single warning source, and it peaked on 2017-05-16.\n- **WARNING, Component `nova.compute.manager`:** 45 entries [E5][E9].\n- **Smaller items:** `keystonemiddleware.auth_token` has 2 ERROR [E4] and 2 WARNING [E5] entries.\n\n## Hypotheses\n\n- The image-cache subsystem is the main area to check. Its periodic cleanup pass fails with disk-info errors, and the warning volume is much larger than the error volume. The failures recur across both days, so they look persistent rather than a single spike.\n- The logs do not show why `qemu-img` fails. A disk-image or storage-access problem is a plausible guess, but it is not established here.\n\n## Unknowns\n\n- **Impact:** The logs cannot establish downtime, customer impact, or financial loss. Matching Log Entries are not incidents.\n- **Root cause:** The sampled messages do not show why `qemu-img` fails or whether the affected disks are damaged.\n- **CRITICAL entries:** Level shows 2 CRITICAL entries [E2], but a message search for \"CRITICAL\" returned 0 [E6]. The content of those 2 entries is unknown.\n- **Missing levels:** 8 entries have no level [E2], so they are excluded from the severity view.\n- **Instance scope:** Sampled periodic-task ERROR lines have no instance_id [E7], so I cannot say how many instances are affected.\n- **Resolution:** The logs do not show whether the errors stopped after 2017-05-17.\n\n## Next Step\n\nAsk the OpenStack Component owner (`nova.virt.libvirt.imagecache` / `oslo_service.periodic_task`) to review the 184 periodic-task ERRORs and the 3,059 image-cache WARNINGs, starting with the 2017-05-16 peak. Priority order:\n1. `oslo_service.periodic_task` ERRORs (184 Log Entries) [E4].\n2. `nova.virt.libvirt.imagecache` WARNINGs (3,059 Log Entries) [E5].\n3. `nova.compute.manager` WARNINGs (45 Log Entries) [E9], then the 2 `keystonemiddleware.auth_token` ERROR entries [E4].",
